Both findings fixed, all four acceptance gates green.

**F1** — copied the `isolateConfig(t)` helper from `cmd/bd/autostart_test.go` into `internal/config/config_test.go` (package `main` can't be imported) and called it from `TestDefaults`. Two things beyond the finding: the environment leaks the same way (viper's prefix is `BD`, config.go:71, so the contract's own `BD_NO_DAEMON=true` still masked the `no-daemon` default after the config was isolated), so the helper now unsets and restores every `BD_*`/`BEADS_*` variable; and the package sweep found two more default-asserting tests, `TestGetMultiRepoConfig` and `TestGetExternalProjects`, which now call it too. Assertions and the repo config untouched.

**F2** — the configured-prefix branch in `upsertIssues` (internal/importer/importer.go:626) now reads `configuredPrefix != "" && config.GetMultiRepoConfig() == nil`, so multi-repo mode falls into the `ExtractIssuePrefix` comparison the empty-prefix case already used, matching `buildAllowedPrefixSet`'s GH#686 short-circuit. No new test: the nearest neighbour, `TestImportCrossPrefixContentMatch`, would need a staged multi-repo viper config, well past a two-line extension.

